From: OpenWrt MT6990 repair <mt6990@local>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mediatek: reclaim MT6990 QDMA to DTX

MT6990 runs QDMA with TX_WB_DDONE clear, so the release DRX pointer is not
the hardware completion boundary used by the vendor driver.  Use the acquire
DTX pointer instead.  The hardware also stores status in the low bits of the
linked-list next pointer; mask those bits before converting it to a virtual
descriptor address.

This restores the two completion rules previously validated on MT6990 and
keeps the generic QDMA path unchanged for all other SoCs.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
@@ -2844,13 +2844,17 @@ static int mtk_poll_tx_qdma(struct mtk_eth *eth, int budget,
 	u32 cpu, dma;
 
 	cpu = ring->last_free_ptr;
-	dma = mtk_r32(eth, reg_map->qdma.drx_ptr);
+	dma = mtk_r32(eth, MTK_HAS_CAPS(eth->soc->caps, MTK_SOC_MT6990) ?
+		      reg_map->qdma.dtx_ptr : reg_map->qdma.drx_ptr);
 
 	desc = mtk_qdma_phys_to_virt(ring, cpu);
 	xdp_frame_bulk_init(&bq);
 
 	while ((cpu != dma) && budget) {
 		u32 next_cpu = desc->txd2;
+
+		if (MTK_HAS_CAPS(eth->soc->caps, MTK_SOC_MT6990))
+			next_cpu &= ~((1U << eth->soc->tx.desc_shift) - 1);
 
 		if (MTK_HAS_CAPS(eth->soc->caps, MTK_SOC_MT6990)) {
 			/* Exact SDK order: DDONE belongs to the release anchor. */
